app Notes
    A tiny web API that stores short notes in a SQLite database.

target python

uses
    sqlite database in "notes.db"

settings
    port 8090
    longest note is 200 characters

thing Note
    id: whole number
    text: short text
    created: when it was added, as text like 2026-10-30 14:05

to add note (text) -> the saved Note
    Save the note with the current time and give it back with its new id.
    Text that is empty (after trimming) or longer than the longest note is refused.

to all notes -> a list of Note
    Every note, newest first.

web
    GET  /notes          -> all notes, as JSON
    POST /notes          -> add note using "text" from the JSON body; answer 201 with the note
    GET  /health         -> {"ok": true}
    A refused note answers 400 with {"error": "..."}.

rules
    a note is never longer than the longest note

test a refused note is not saved
    adding a note with only spaces fails, and the number of notes stays the same

on start
    Make sure the notes table exists, print "Notes API on port 8090", and start the web API.
